  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\">Olympia is the first iteration of the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-the-radix-public-network-and-radix-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Public Network</strong></a>, commonly referred to as “mainnet”.&nbsp;</p><p id=\"\">Olympia includes the foundational technologies that act as the basis for all future Radix releases and allows the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-the-radix-community\"><strong id=\"\">Radix</strong> <strong id=\"\">Community</strong></a> to start taking advantage of the most fundamental <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-radix\"><strong id=\"\">Radix</strong></a> features.&nbsp;</p><p id=\"\">Olympia lays the foundation upon which all future versions of the Radix Public Network will be built.&nbsp;</p><p id=\"\">Radix has delivered three pieces of software to support the Olympia mainnet.</p><figure id=\"\" class=\"w-richtext-figure-type-image w-richtext-align-center\" data-rt-type=\"image\" data-rt-align=\"center\"><div id=\"\"><img id=\"\" alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/60540b6d30224a7cb015203a/69eb24d31b0eed71608c4ef6_60ed79021ad15778a1e55921_NlC8meg0RhXxHFiU7Uro0XpcdskLbvMDTqktI8x4H5Tu53X0lpi8aH3nB7xKHdLaidtQqzbB9q41zg3VmihO5qtmyPNxu0jzXUMSomhb-fkeVWCpHW4sM4Q7FhADMrGO7vRRsN0z.png\" width=\"auto\" height=\"auto\" loading=\"auto\"></div></figure><p id=\"\"><br></p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">1 </strong><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-radix-node-software\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Node</strong></a>: The Radix Node is the key software that runs the Radix Public Network and provides useful <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-apis-are-relevant-to-the-radix-public-network\"><strong id=\"\">API</strong></a> endpoints for things like wallets, depending on its configuration.</p><p id=\"\">Once installed, the Node may be run in one of two modes:</p><p id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-validator-node-2\"><strong id=\"\">Validator Node</strong></a></p><p id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-full-node-2\"><strong id=\"\">Full Node</strong></a></p><p id=\"\">You can learn more about the difference between these node modes <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-a-full-node-and-validator-node\"><strong id=\"\">here</strong></a>.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">2 </strong><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-to-completely-reset-your-desktop-wallet-by-deleting-the-keystore\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Desktop Wallet</strong></a><strong id=\"\"> </strong>- Used for storing, transacting, and <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-to-stake-and-unstake-xrd-in-the-desktop-wallet\"><strong id=\"\">staking</strong></a> <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-the-xrd-and-exrd-tokens\"><strong id=\"\">XRD tokens</strong></a>. It makes it easy for anyone to stake and unstake XRD to Radix validators and receive incentive <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-network-emissions\"><strong id=\"\">emissions</strong></a>. It is available on Windows, Mac, and Linux.&nbsp;</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">3 </strong><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-to-use-the-radix-explorer\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Explorer</strong></a><strong id=\"\"> </strong>- Provides a list of all nodes that have registered to be <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-validator-node\"><strong id=\"\">validator nodes</strong></a><strong id=\"\"> </strong>and are available for staking, along with information about each one to help guide choices of which validators to stake to.</p><p id=\"\">‍<br></p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further Reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-can-i-do-on-the-olympia-mainnet\"><strong id=\"\">What can I do on the Olympia mainnet?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-to-set-up-your-wallet\"><strong id=\"\">How to Set Up Your Wallet</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-to-check-your-token-balances\"><strong id=\"\">How to Check Your token Balance</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-to-stake-and-unstake-xrd-in-the-desktop-wallet\"><strong id=\"\">How to Stake and Unstake XRD in the Desktop Wallet</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-the-radix-roadmap\"><strong id=\"\">What is the Radix roadmap?</strong></a></li></ul>",
